actualFindings.suggestion:
Convert the test to async and use Vitest's async-aware form: `await expect(processPayment(mockPayload)).resolves.toBeDefined()` to assert it doesn't reject, or use `await expect(processPayment(mockPayload)).rejects.toThrow()` when testing for expected rejections. Example fix:

```ts
it('should not throw on valid input', async () => {
  await expect(processPayment(mockPayload)).resolves.toBeDefined();
});
```
